@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title PLANNED — Harness choice cache: three axes, declared per def, prompted once

actor "Operator" as OP

node "defs/<target>/harness.manifest" as MAN <<host>> {
  component "capabilities:\negress · credentials\nproviders · addons" as CAP <<app>>
}

node "cmd/proveo run <target>" as CLI <<host>> {
  component "resolve()\nflag > cache > prompt > default" as RES <<app>>
  component "choice TUI\n3 radio rows + .env header" as TUI <<app>>
  component "validate against capabilities" as VAL <<app>>
}

database "~/.proveo/agent-settings.yml\nper target + manifest fingerprint\negress · credentials · addons\nauthVar · models" as CACHE <<db>>
component "fingerprint mismatch\n→ discard, re-prompt" as STALE <<error>>
component "headless (no TTY)\n→ never prompt, take default" as HEADLESS <<error>>

CAP ARROW_MAIN VAL : the only source of valid cells
OP ARROW_MAIN RES : ""--egress-mode"" · ""--credentials"" · ""--browser"" · ""PROVEO_DIND""
RES ARROW_MAIN CACHE : read
CACHE ARROW_ERROR STALE : manifest changed
RES ARROW_MAIN TUI : cache miss or stale
TUI ARROW_MAIN OP : one prompt, three rows
TUI ARROW_QUEUE CACHE : persist the answer
RES ARROW_ERROR HEADLESS
RES ARROW_MAIN VAL

note right of CAP
  **The matrix is data, not code.** Cursor's constraint lives in
  ""cmd/proveo/main.go"" today as ""if target == 'cursor'"". Declaring it
  here deletes that special case and makes the choice space
  inspectable per def.

  ""egress: [open]"" — cursor pins its TLS; every intercepting tier
  breaks it.
  ""credentials: [forward]"" — nothing can be injected into that TLS.
  ""providers: [anthropic]"" — claudecode reads only its own key and
  OAuth token.
  ""addons"" — derived by default: DinD iff ""dind: true"", browser iff an
  ""images:"" key ends ""-browser"". claudecode therefore shows no DinD row.
end note

note bottom of VAL
  **""providers"" also fixes a live bug.** In a brokered tier
  ""provider.KeyVars()"" sentinel-injects EVERY detected key, so
  ""brokerProvider"" sees two or more, refuses to pin, and the agent
  gets the ""proveo-brokered"" sentinel — the provider then answers 403.
  Filtering detection through the def's declared providers means a
  stray key for a harness that cannot use it never enters the set.
end note

note bottom of TUI
  **One prompt, three rows.** Header first: ""\.env"" as loaded —
  **names only** for secrets (manifest ""env[].secret"" ∪
  ""provider\.KeyVars()""), ""key=value"" for the rest
  (""entrypoint\.ConfigVars"" ∪ manifest ""config"").

  **A single-option axis is not a choice, so its row is dropped.** Cursor,
  fixed to open+forward, would otherwise show two controls that cannot
  move. Where a choice DOES exist, every option stays visible and the
  unavailable ones are greyed **with the reason on the row** — that is
  the dind case, which depends on the two axes above it.

  Hiding a row costs the gate its input: ""gateAddons"" falls back to the
  already-resolved axis value, and capabilities are applied BEFORE the
  prompt so both the fallback and the pre-selection reflect the def.

  ""go-fuzzyfinder"" is a fuzzy list picker and cannot express a radio
  grid; ""tcell"" is already vendored beneath it, so the form is a small
  custom widget.
end note

note right of RES
  **The prompt always appears.** A remembered answer SEEDS the selection;
  it never replaces the form. Silently entering a cached tier hid the
  security posture of the run — the operator must see, and be able to
  change, what they are launching.

  **Four axes, shown only when there is something to decide:** network
  tier, credential handling, which credential (when the pinned provider
  accepts more than one the operator holds), and add-ons.

  ""review"" is offered on a Linux host with a local daemon and greyed
  elsewhere with the reason — 'linux only', or 'needs a local docker daemon'
  for a remote ""DOCKER_HOST"". Naming the constraint beats a blanket 'coming
  soon': the tier is not unfinished, its transport is platform-bound. See
  ""_spec/internal/reviewgate/pty-review-proxy.puml"".

  **Resolution order.** An explicit flag always wins, and when a
  prompt does appear the flag value is **pre-selected** rather than
  bypassing the row. Otherwise: a valid cache enters automatically
  (the point of the feature), else prompt, else the manifest default.
end note

note bottom of STALE
  **Cached choices do not survive a manifest change.** The cache
  stores a fingerprint of the def's ""capabilities"" block; any change
  discards the entry and re-prompts, rather than silently dropping a
  now-invalid add-on or keeping a tier the def no longer allows.
end note

note bottom of CACHE
  **Models are remembered too, and are not a form row.** ""targets.<t>.models""
  records the last used ""main"" / ""editor"" / ""small"" as **canonical** ids, so a
  session that mixes providers is reproducible without retyping three env
  vars. Canonical rather than harness-specific: the translated spelling would
  pin the entry to whatever the catalog said the day it was written, and a
  synced correction would never reach it.

  Precedence matches every other axis — **explicit env or flag > cached >
  unset** — and a cached id that no longer resolves degrades to a warning
  and is dropped. proveo must not hard-fail on a file it wrote itself.

  Unlike the three axes, models are not radio cells: they are typed values
  with an open range, so they appear read-only in the prompt header beside
  the workspace and ""\.env"". The radio grid stays radios.

  Resolution is specified in ""_spec/internal/provider/model-resolution\.puml"".
end note

note bottom of HEADLESS
  E2E, CI and cron must never block on a human: with no TTY the
  resolver takes the manifest default and logs the choice it made.
end note
@enduml
